  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Montana received $52.4M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government made 360 awards in the state, with an average award size of $146K. Obligations fell 96.2% year over year. The Department of the Interior accounted for the largest share, obligating $28.4M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $11.3M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $6.1M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligation, receiving $21.9M, and PAULSEN CONSTRUCTION LLC is the single largest contractor with $21.6M in obligations. FY2027 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Historical context shows much larger full-year obligations in prior years, with FY26 at $1.4B and FY25 at $1.1B, so current-year totals represent a small slice of typical annual spending. Use the FY2027 to date figures for current activity and the fiscal-year listings for trend context.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $52.4M compared with $1.4B in FY26 and $1.1B in FY25. Fiscal-year obligations were $1.1B in FY24, $1B in FY23, and $925M in FY22. Obligations fell 96.2% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors drive federal spending in Montana this year?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior leads buying with $28.4M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $11.3M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $6.1M. PAULSEN CONSTRUCTION LLC is the largest vendor with $21.6M, BRIDGER AEROSPACE GROUP, LLC follows with $5.3M, and BRIDGER AIR TANKER LLC has $3M."
      }
    ]
